{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"invariants","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:a6adce2af176e8100e5f874b46c0da40fde53f56940f925c820d53da0079f829/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7","passage_ref":"sha256:1fd49f692320db9f27935d8a5c8bc9bc22bddf38904cfd9fa8def31510d242d5/papers/long.md/sha256:a6adce2af176e8100e5f874b46c0da40fde53f56940f925c820d53da0079f829/papers/long.json/passages/invariants","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&paper=long&passage=invariants","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&paper=long&passage=invariants","span":{"end_byte":243228,"end_line":2799,"start_byte":213625,"start_line":2408},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&view=arguments&node=long.record-257hg-i4&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&node=long.record-257hg-i4&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&node=long.record-257hg-i4&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&view=arguments&node=long.record-257hg-i4&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&ref=sha256%3A72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696%2Fnodes%2Flong.record-257hg-i4","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257hg-i4"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257hg-i4"],"id":"long.record-257hg-i4","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.120 (A sufficient inequality for a safe skip)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.120, p. 77, label record:257hg-i4","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $k,u,L\\ge1$ be integers, set $a=2L-(2^k-1)u$, and suppose $a>0$. For the skipped rational remainder $\\rho=u/(2L)$, $\\rho\\le2^{-k}$ is equivalent to $u\\le a$, whereas\n$$\n2u\\le3a\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\rho<R_k.\n$$\nThe latter implication uses the three-term lower bound above. More explicitly, with $t=2^k\\ge2$,\n$$\n\\left(\\frac1t+\\frac1{3t^2}+\\frac1{7t^3}\\right)\n       -\\frac3{3t-1}\n =\\frac{2t-3}{21t^3(3t-1)}>0.\n$$\nThe inequality $2u\\le3a$ gives $\\rho\\le3/(3t-1)$, proving the claim. The first two terms alone would not prove this comparison. This is a sufficient exclusion of the current tail-mass deficit, not an exact test for membership in the remaining achievement set.*\n\n*The sufficient condition is weaker than $u\\le a$. A realizable example is $(k,u,L,a)=(2,7,13,5)$; it passes $2u\\le3a$ but not $u\\le a$. The linked scalar example $(u,a)=(3,2)$ proves strict containment of the inequalities, but is not integral rational data for this substitution. For comparison, the exact mass threshold is $a/u\\ge R_k^{-1}-(2^k-1)$; its right-hand side lies strictly between $0$ and $2/3$. None of these comparisons asserts that the half-greedy orbit satisfies the sufficient inequality at every skipped rank.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_dyadic_skip_test_iff%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_dyadic_skip_test_iff%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_dyadic_skip_test_iff"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_mass_threshold%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_mass_threshold%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_exact_mass_threshold"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257hg-i4","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_sharp_gives_three_over_three_t_sub_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257hg-i4%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_sharp_gives_three_over_three_t_sub_one%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to